  ├───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mconsole.error("Validation error:", [39m   │ [38;5;153mlog.warn('login.validation_failed', { username, error: validation.error[39m │
  │ [38;5;153m...)[39m                                  │ [38;5;153m })[39m                                                                     │
  └───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Plus two new global handlers, installed in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m (not [38;5;153mlogger.js[39m, per the constraint above):
  [38;5;153mwindow.addEventListener('error', ...)[39m → [38;5;153mlog.error('uncaught.error', { message, source, lineno, colno, stack })[39m, and
  [38;5;153m'unhandledrejection'[39m → [38;5;153mlog.error('uncaught.rejection', { reason })[39m.

  Two judgment calls worth your veto: I'm [1mdowngrading the validation failure from [38;5;153merror[39m to [38;5;153mwarn[0m, because a user
  forgetting a field is not an application fault and shouldn't pollute an error feed. And I'm logging [38;5;153mresult.success[39m
  rather than the whole [38;5;153mresult[39m object, so the record shape doesn't silently change if [38;5;153mlogin()[39m stops being a stub.

  [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m are untouched.

  [1m4. Error handling[0m

  The logger must never break the app: the sink call is wrapped in [38;5;153mtry/catch[39m and a throwing sink is swallowed. A logging
  failure taking down a login form would be worse than the bug you were chasing.

  [1m5. Testing ([38;5;153mtest/logger.test.js[39m, new)[0m

  [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m gets [38;5;153m"scripts": { "test": "node --test" }[39m — no dependencies. Tests cover: redaction at top level, nested,
  inside arrays, and case-insensitive keys; non-sensitive fields surviving untouched; the cycle guard; level filtering
  above and below threshold; record shape and a stable [38;5;153msessionId[39m across calls; a custom sink receiving records; and a
  throwing sink not propagating.

